 If the proposed metadata cannot fit existing bounded SourceCode and fact limits, or existing repository semantics cannot preserve it losslessly, return a specification amendment before coding a clinical-model or storage redesign.
 
+## Shared values and prevention of duplicate charting
+
+RF2 is another view and entry point into the shared patient record, not a second weight or fluid database. The same source observation may appear in renal, hemodynamics, nutrition, medication review and handover while retaining one exact fact identity/revision and history. Repeated display is not a second measurement.
+
+Before implementation, inventory existing weight and fluid representations, concept/source codes, ownership, collection identifiers and exact lookup paths at the approved baseline. Record a bounded mapping in the implementation package. Reuse the existing authoritative entry/correction path when available; do not build a competing renal path. If an existing generic weight observation needs another kind of write contract, leave its correction with its existing owner and link to it rather than cloning it into a circulatory event. If that path is unavailable and completing the approved journey requires a new legacy authoring contract, request a specification amendment. Missing typed purpose/method remains unavailable; do not derive it from a narrative.
+
+For weight, show existing source records before offering new entry. The user chooses Use existing measurement, Correct this measurement or Record genuinely new measurement. Select existing by repository/patient/encounter and exact kind/ID/revision/digest, not by the displayed number. Sharing a measured weight for dosing or fluid review creates an exact contextual link, not another quantity. A separately asserted dosing-weight value or a different collection remains separately labelled with its provenance; neither automatically replaces a measured weight. There is no universal patient weight field whose latest number silently overwrites every purpose.
+
+Use an explicit source collection identifier when available. Under one transaction, replaying an existing source identifier with identical content returns the same fact; conflicting content requires explicit correction/conflict handling, never another automatic insertion. Preserve the distinct pending-request identity/idempotency rules. When collection identity is unavailable, show plausible overlaps from the bounded loaded view and require an explicit new-collection assertion with a reason; describe these as possible duplicates, not a complete cross-system search. Same value/time alone is not proof of duplication, and different units are not converted to search for matches. Do not merge genuine repeat measurements or fabricate missing source IDs.
+
+For fluids, retain one source event referenced by each applicable view. A fluid challenge, administered volume, interval total and cumulative balance can overlap in accounting without being identical facts. Show the source-declared relationship when available and a possible-overlap limitation otherwise. Do not copy an event from hemodynamics into renal charting, add components to their reported totals, or automatically infer equivalence/containment from coincident values or times. Interval overlap and undocumented gaps remain visible; RF2 does not calculate a reconciled balance.
+
+Corrections append to the original owning fact identity. Each refreshed view shows the same corrected source or an explicitly older cutoff. Old notes and saved handover keep their exact original revision references; they are not rewritten. Repository/patient/encounter/cutoff boundaries continue to apply to these shared values.
+
 ## Charting and correction workflow
 
-1. Open Renal and fluid review for the shared patient, encounter, window and cutoff. Choose Record urine, Record fluid or Record weight. These are local synthetic actions, distinct from clinical execution.
+1. Open Renal and fluid review for the shared patient, encounter, window and cutoff. Choose Use existing evidence or Record genuinely new urine/fluid/weight evidence after reviewing existing sources. These are local synthetic actions, distinct from clinical execution.
 2. Show required fields beside the entry: source category, quantity or explicit missing state, raw unit, source time/interval assertions, actor and uncertainty. Unknown context must be selectable; no positive-quality, verified-clock or measured-status defaults.
 3. Urine/fluid records use an explicit interval or a clearly marked point event. Partial or unknown bounds remain partial/unknown and are not turned into an hour. Reject contradictory exact start/end ordering using the accepted exact-time machinery; do not round timestamps or guess local timezone. Do not calculate duration or rate. Weight uses its own point/unknown time and explicit measured/reported/dosing purpose; measurement method may be unavailable.
 4. Present a validated review showing scope, proposed exact identity, amounts, intervals, raw context and limitations before the explicit save. Validation is not a saved confirmation.
